---
layout: default
body_classes:
  - docs
  - doc-page
editable: true
---
{%- comment -%}
  Which license the page states: the handbook is share-alike, the rest of
  the documentation is share-alike and non-commercial.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign inHandbook = false -%}
{%- if page.url contains '/docs/handbook/' -%}
  {%- assign inHandbook = true -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%}
  A page adapted from Google's style guide says so with `google: true`, which
  reads the source page off its own filename. Where the two differ, name
  Google's slug instead: `google: inclusive-documentation`.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if google -%}
  {%- assign googleSlug = page.fileSlug -%}
  {%- unless google == true -%}
    {%- assign googleSlug = google -%}
  {%- endunless -%}
  {%- assign googleUrl = 'https://developers.google.com/style/'
    | append: googleSlug
  -%}
{%- endif -%}
<main class='flex-shrink-0'>
  <article>
    <header class='doc-head'>
      <div class='wrap'>
        {% include 'breadcrumb.liquid' %}
        <h1 class='doc-title'>{{ title }}</h1>
        {%- if key_point %}
          <p class='doc-key'>{{ key_point }}</p>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class='doc-body'>
      <div class='wrap'>
        <div class='doc-prose'>{{ content }}</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <footer class='doc-foot'>
    <div class='wrap doc-foot-grid'>
      <div class='doc-terms-block'>
        {%- comment -%}
          The buttons name the terms the sentence below spells out, so they
          are decorative here and the sentence carries the link.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <p class='doc-cc' aria-hidden='true'>
          {% include 'assets/img/cc/cc-logo.svg' %}
          {% include 'assets/img/cc/cc-by.svg' %}
          {%- unless inHandbook %}
            {% include 'assets/img/cc/cc-nc.svg' %}
          {%- endunless %}
          {% include 'assets/img/cc/cc-sa.svg' %}
        </p>
        <p class='doc-terms'>
          {%- if google %}
            Portions of this page are reproduced from work
            <a
              href='https://developers.google.com/site-policies'
              rel='nofollow noopener noreferrer'
              >shared by Google</a
            >
            under
            <a
              href='https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/'
              rel='license nofollow noopener noreferrer'
              >CC BY 4.0</a
            >, from
            <a
              href='{{ googleUrl }}'
              title='Google developer documentation style guide'
              rel='nofollow noopener noreferrer'
              >the original page</a
            >.
          {%- endif %}
          Except where noted, this page is published under
          {%- if inHandbook %}
            <a
              href='https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/'
              rel='license nofollow noopener noreferrer'
              >CC BY-SA 4.0</a
            >.
          {%- else %}
            <a
              href='https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/'
              rel='license nofollow noopener noreferrer'
              >CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a
            >.
          {%- endif %}
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class='doc-foot-aside'>
        {%- assign updated = page.inputPath | gitLastUpdated -%}
        {%- if updated %}
          <p class='doc-updated'>
            Last updated
            <time datetime='{{ updated | date: "%Y-%m-%d" }}'>
              {{- updated | date: '%Y-%m-%d' -}}
            </time>
            UTC
          </p>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if editable != false %}
          <p class='doc-edit'>
            <a
              href='https://github.com/OpenINF/openinf.github.io/edit/{{ repoBranch }}/{{ page.inputPath | remove_first: './' }}'
            >
              {% include 'assets/img/octicons/pencil.svg' %}
              Improve this page
            </a>
          </p>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>
</main>
